The coordinator started the JVM lane for #8692 on `33f7785cf5`. It accepts these changes and nothing else:
- the identity change (token, plus pair v322/v321);
- completion changes where an on-demand Kotlin artifact now admits instead of exceeding its staged budget, each one named by site;
- no SQL change;
- `work50` equal except on the moved sites.

Any answer that becomes less complete fails the lane. Master is now at pair v315/v314 after batch #8690, and v322 is still above it and above every ready head.

Waiting on:
- The #8692 lane verdict and review.
- #8682 in the merge queue.
- Your answer on #8580. I recommend measuring first.

The reviewer accepts the design. One test change is required: the witness must assert the expected outcome, not only that the two results are equal. The test must also gain a case that has to refuse, for every origin, stored rows included. Three follow-ups come with it:
- check whether the C++ census undercounts nested entries;
- confirm whether this PR also fixes #8624;
- post on #8665 which Scala golden lines, if any, come from #8586.

The Scala question is cheap. I have the actual Scala output from two runs: #8617 plus master `a8316c4aa6` without #8586, and #8586 plus master `96a4dc7dbb`. If they're identical, #8586 contributes none of those lines.
